<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
<title>Form 8801</title>
<style>
  @page { size: A4; margin: 0; }
  .page {
    width: 794px; height: 1123px;
    padding: 50px 60px; box-sizing: border-box;
    overflow: hidden; page-break-after: always;
    position: relative;
  }
  .page:last-child { page-break-after: auto; }
  body {
    font-family: "DejaVu Serif", "Liberation Serif", Georgia, "Helvetica", Arial, sans-serif;
    font-size: 10pt;
  }
  h1, h2, h3 {
    font-weight: bold;
  }
  .section-header {
    font-weight: bold;
    margin-top: 15px;
    margin-bottom: 5px;
  }
  .line-item {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    margin-bottom: 5px;
  }
  .label {
    flex-basis: 70%;
  }
  .value {
    flex-basis: 30%;
    text-align: right;
  }
  .two-column {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    margin-bottom: 15px;
  }
  .two-column > div {
    width: 48%;
  }
  .table-container {
    width: 100%;
    border-collapse: collapse;
    margin-top: 10px;
  }
  .table-container td {
    padding: 4px 0;
    border-bottom: 1px solid #ccc;
  }
  .table-container tr:last-child td {
    border-bottom: none;
  }
</style>
</head>
<body>

<div class="page">
  <div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: flex-start;">
    <div>
      <h1 style="font-size: 16pt; margin: 0;">Form 8801</h1>
      <div style="margin-top: 10px;">
        Department of the Treasury<br>
        Internal Revenue Service (99)
      </div>
      <div style="margin-top: 20px;">
        Name(s) shown on return
      </div>
    </div>
    <div style="text-align: right;">
      <div style="font-size: 14pt; font-weight: bold;">OMB No. 1545-1073</div>
      <div style="font-size: 12pt;">
        <div style="font-weight: bold;">2000</div>
        <div style="font-size: 10pt;">Attestation</div>
        <div style="font-size: 10pt;">Sequence No. 74</div>
        <div style="font-size: 10pt;">Identifying number</div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <h2 style="margin-top: 30px;">Credit For Prior Year Minimum Tax—Individuals, Estates, and Trusts</h2>
  <div style="margin-top: 10px;">
    <span data-field="attach_to_tax_return">{{ attach_to_tax_return }}</span>
  </div>

  <div class="section-header">Part I Net Minimum Tax on Exclusion Items</div>

  <div style="margin-top: 15px;">
    <div class="line-item">
      <div class="label">1 Combine lines 16 through 18 of your 1999 Form 6251. Estates and trusts, see instructions.</div>
      <div class="value"><span data-field="line_1">{{ line_1 }}</span></div>
    </div>
    <div class="line-item">
      <div class="label">2 Enter adjustments and preferences treated as exclusion items. See instructions.</div>
      <div class="value"><span data-field="line_2">{{ line_2 }}</span></div>
    </div>
    <div class="line-item">
      <div class="label">3 Minimum tax credit net operating loss deduction. See instructions.</div>
      <div class="value"><span data-field="line_3">{{ line_3 }}</span></div>
    </div>
    <div class="line-item">
      <div class="label">4 Combine lines 1, 2, and 3. If zero or less, enter -0 here and on line 15 and go to Part II. If more than $165,000 and you were married filing separately for 1999, see instructions.</div>
      <div class="value"><span data-field="line_4">{{ line_4 }}</span></div>
    </div>
    <div class="line-item">
      <div class="label">5 Enter: $45,000 if married filing jointly or qualifying widow(er) for (1999); $33,750 if single or head of household for 1999; or $22,500 if married filing separately for 1999. Estates and trusts, enter $22,500.</div>
      <div class="value"><span data-field="line_5">{{ line_5 }}</span></div>
    </div>
    <div class="line-item">
      <div class="label">6 Enter: $150,000 if married filing jointly or qualifying widow(er) for (1999); $112,500 if single or head of household for 1999; or $75,000 if married filing separately for 1999. Estates and trusts, enter $75,000.</div>
      <div class="value"><span data-field="line_6">{{ line_6 }}</span></div>
    </div>
    <div class="line-item">
      <div class="label">7 Subtract line 6 from line 4. If zero or less, enter -0 here and on line 8 and go to line 9.</div>
      <div class="value"><span data-field="line_7">{{ line_7 }}</span></div>
    </div>
    <div class="line-item">
      <div class="label">8 Multiply line 7 by 25% (25).</div>
      <div class="value"><span data-field="line_8">{{ line_8 }}</span></div>
    </div>
    <div class="line-item">
      <div class="label">9 Subtract line 8 from line 5 if zero or less, enter -0. If this form is for a child under age 14, see instructions.</div>
      <div class="value"><span data-field="line_9">{{ line_9 }}</span></div>
    </div>
    <div class="line-item">
      <div class="label">10 Subtract line 9 from line 4. If zero or less, enter -0 here and on line 15 and go to Part II. Form 1040NR filers, see instructions.</div>
      <div class="value"><span data-field="line_10">{{ line_10 }}</span></div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="section-header" style="margin-top: 25px;">Part II Minimum Tax Credit and Carryforward to 2001</div>

  <div style="margin-top: 15px;">
    <div class="line-item">
      <div class="label">11 If for 1999 you reported capital gain distributions directly on Form 1040, line 13, or corrected Form 1040, line 24, or Form 1041 and have not filed Form 27 of Schedule D (Form 1040) line 24 or line 26 of Schedule D (Form 1041) or have not used the losses they had claimed, go to Part II of Form 8801 to figure the amount to enter on this line. All others: Multiply line 26 by 26% (26). If line 15 is $175,000 or less if single, head of household, married filing jointly, qualifying widow(er), or an estate or trust for 1999; or $87,500 or less if married filing separately for 1999. Otherwise, multiply line 10 by 28% (28) and subtract from the result: $3,500 if single, head of household, married filing jointly, qualifying widow(er), or an estate or trust for 1999; or $1,750 if married filing separately for 1999.</div>
      <div class="value"><span data-field="line_11">{{ line_11 }}</span></div>
    </div>
    <div class="line-item">
      <div class="label">12 Minimum tax foreign tax credit on exclusion items. See instructions.</div>
      <div class="value"><span data-field="line_12">{{ line_12 }}</span></div>
    </div>
    <div class="line-item">
      <div class="label">13 Tentative minimum tax on exclusion items. Subtract line 12 from line 11.</div>
      <div class="value"><span data-field="line_13">{{ line_13 }}</span></div>
    </div>
    <div class="line-item">
      <div class="label">14 Enter the amount from your 1999 Form 6251, line 27, or Form 1041, Schedule I, line 38.</div>
      <div class="value"><span data-field="line_14">{{ line_14 }}</span></div>
    </div>
    <div class="line-item">
      <div class="label">15 Net minimum tax on exclusion items. Subtract line 14 from line 13. If zero or less, enter -0.</div>
      <div class="value"><span data-field="line_15">{{ line_15 }}</span></div>
    </div>
  </div>

</div>

<div class="page">
  <div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: flex-start;">
    <div style="width: 50%;">
      <div class="section-header">Part III Line 11 Computation Using Maximum Capital Gains Rates</div>
      <div style="margin-top: 15px;">
        <div class="line-item">
          <div class="label">Caution: If you did not complete Schedule D (Form 1040) for 1999 because you reported capital gain distributions directly on Form 1040, line 13, see the instructions before you complete this part. If you are an individual and you did not complete Part IV of your 1999 Schedule D (Form 1041), complete lines 19 through 26 of that Schedule D before completing this part.</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div style="width: 50%; text-align: right;">
      <div style="font-size: 10pt;">Page 2</div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="section-header" style="margin-top: 25px;">General Instructions</div>
  <div style="margin-top: 15px;">
    <div class="line-item">
      <div class="label">Purpose of Form</div>
      <div class="value"></div>
    </div>
    <div class="line-item">
      <div class="label">Use Form 8801 if you are an individual, estate, or trust to figure the minimum tax credit for your tax years and to figure any minimum tax credit carryforward.</div>
      <div class="value"></div>
    </div>
    <div class="line-item">
      <div class="label">Who Should File</div>
      <div class="value"></div>
    </div>
    <div class="line-item">
      <div class="label">Complete Form 8801 if you are an individual, estate, or trust that had:</div>
      <div class="value"></div>
    </div>
    <div class="line-item">
      <div class="label">An AMT liability in 1999 and</div>
      <div class="value"></div>
    </div>
    <div class="line-item">
      <div class="label">An AMT liability in 1999 and</div>
      <div class="value"></div>
    </div>
    <div class="line-item">
      <div class="label">A minimum tax credit carryforward from 1999 to 2000, or</div>
      <div class="value"></div>
    </div>
    <div class="line-item">
      <div class="label">A nonconventional source fuel credit that was claimed in 1999 (see the instructions for line 20).</div>
      <div class="value"></div>
    </div>
    <div class="line-item">
      <div class="label">File Form 8801 only if line 21 is more than zero.</div>
      <div class="value"></div>
    </div>
    <div class="line-item">
      <div class="label">Specific Instructions</div>
      <div class="value"></div>
    </div>
    <div class="line-item">
      <div class="label">The AMT is attributable to two types of adjustments and preferences: deferral items and exclusion items. Deferral items (for example, the standard deduction) generally don't cause a permanent difference in taxable income over time. Exclusion items (for example, the standard deduction) generally do not cause a permanent difference. The minimum tax credit is allowed only for the AMT attributable to deferral items.</div>
      <div class="value"></div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="section-header" style="margin-top: 25px;">Line 1–Estates and Trusts</div>
  <div style="margin-top: 15px;">
    <div class="line-item">
      <div class="label">Skip lines 1 through 3 of Form 8801. Complete Parts I and II of Form 8801.</div>
      <div class="value"></div>
    </div>
    <div class="line-item">
      <div class="label">For Part III, take into account any adjustments arising from deferral items. If the amount on Schedule I, line 3 is this page for how to figure the amount to enter on line 11.</div>
      <div class="value"></div>
    </div>
    <div class="line-item">
      <div class="label">Line 2: Enter on this line the adjustments and preferences treated as exclusions. Exclusion items are your AMT adjustments and preferences for the standard deduction, itemized deductions (including any investment interest expense reported on Schedule A), and the minimum tax credit carryforward.</div>
      <div class="value"></div>
    </div>
    <div class="line-item">
      <div class="label">Line 3: If you are an estate or trust, enter the amount from Form 6251, line 29. Do not include any adjustments or preferences that are attributable to deferral items.</div>
      <div class="value"></div>
    </div>
    <div class="line-item">
      <div class="label">Line 4: If your status was married filing separately for 1999, enter the amount from Form 6251, line 30. If you were married filing jointly or qualifying widow(er) for 1999, enter the amount from Form 6251, line 31. If you were single or head of household for 1999, enter the amount from Form 6251, line 32.</div>
      <div class="value"></div>
    </div>
    <div class="line-item">
      <div class="label">Line 5: If you are a child under age 14 January 1, 2000, and you were married filing separately for 1999, enter the amount from Form 6251, line 33. If you were single or head of household for 1999, enter the amount from Form 6251, line 34. If you were married filing jointly or qualifying widow(er) for 1999, enter the amount from Form 6251, line 35.</div>
      <div class="value"></div>
    </div>
    <div class="line-item">
      <div class="label">Line 6: Enter the amount from Form 6251, line 36.</div>
      <div class="value"></div>
    </div>
    <div class="line-item">
      <div class="label">Line 7: Subtract line 6 from line 4. If zero or less, enter -0.</div>
      <div class="value"></div>
    </div>
    <div class="line-item">
      <div class="label">Line 8: Multiply line 7 by 25% (25).</div>
      <div class="value"></div>
    </div>
    <div class="line-item">
      <div class="label">Line 9: Subtract line 8 from line 5 if zero or less, enter -0.</div>
      <div class="value"></div>
    </div>
    <div class="line-item">
      <div class="label">Line 10: If you filed Form 1040NR for 1999 and had a net gain on the disposition of U.S. real property interests, line 10 cannot be less than the smaller of that line or line 4.</div>
      <div class="value"></div>
    </div>
    <div class="line-item">
      <div class="label">Line 11: The minimum tax foreign tax credit on exclusion items (MTFCE) is the smaller of the tentative minimum tax credit (TMTCE) or the MTFCE. Follow these steps to figure your MTFCE.</div>
      <div class="value"></div>
    </div>
    <div class="line-item">
      <div class="label">Line 12: Enter the amount from Form 6251, line 27.</div>
      <div class="value"></div>
    </div>
    <div class="line-item">
      <div class="label">Line 13: Tentative minimum tax on exclusion items. Subtract line 12 from line 11.</div>
      <div class="value"></div>
    </div>
    <div class="line-item">
      <div class="label">Line 14: Enter the amount from your 1999 Form 6251, line 38.</div>
      <div class="value"></div>
    </div>
    <div class="line-item">
      <div class="label">Line 15: Net minimum tax on exclusion items. Subtract line 14 from line 13. If zero or less, enter -0.</div>
      <div class="value"></div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="section-header" style="margin-top: 25px;">Line 20</div>
  <div style="margin-top: 15px;">
    <div class="line-item">
      <div class="label">Enter the total of any nonconventional source fuel credit and 1999 unallowed qualified electric vehicle credit. See instructions.</div>
      <div class="value"><span data-field="line_20">{{ line_20 }}</span></div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="section-header" style="margin-top: 25px;">Line 21</div>
  <div style="margin-top: 15px;">
    <div class="line-item">
      <div class="label">Combine lines 18, 19, 20, and 22 if zero or less, stop here and see instructions.</div>
      <div class="value"><span data-field="line_21">{{ line_21 }}</span></div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="section-header" style="margin-top: 25px;">Line 22</div>
  <div style="margin-top: 15px;">
    <div class="line-item">
      <div class="label">Enter your 2000 regular income tax liability minus allowable credits. See instructions.</div>
      <div class="value"><span data-field="line_22">{{ line_22 }}</span></div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="section-header" style="margin-top: 25px;">Line 23</div>
  <div style="margin-top: 15px;">
    <div class="line-item">
      <div class="label">Enter the amount from your 2000 Form 1041, Schedule I, line 37.</div>
      <div class="value"><span data-field="line_23">{{ line_23 }}</span></div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="section-header" style="margin-top: 25px;">Line 24</div>
  <div style="margin-top: 15px;">
    <div class="line-item">
      <div class="label">Subtract line 23 from line 22. If zero or less, enter -0.</div>
      <div class="value"><span data-field="line_24">{{ line_24 }}</span></div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="section-header" style="margin-top: 25px;">Line 25</div>
  <div style="margin-top: 15px;">
    <div class="line-item">
      <div class="label">Minimum tax credit. Enter the smaller of line 21 or line 24. Also enter this amount on your 2000 Form 1040, line 49; Form 1040NR, line 48, or Form 1041, line 25.</div>
      <div class="value"><span data-field="line_25">{{ line_25 }}</span></div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="section-header" style="margin-top: 25px;">Line 26</div>
  <div style="margin-top: 15px;">
    <div class="line-item">
      <div class="label">Minimum tax credit carryforward to 2001. Subtract line 25 from line 21. Keep a record of this amount because you may use it in future years.</div>
      <div class="value"><span data-field="line_26">{{ line_26 }}</span></div>
    </div>
  </div>

</div>

<div class="page">
  <div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: flex-start;">
    <div style="width: 50%;">
      <div class="section-header">Part III Line 11 Computation Using Maximum Capital Gains Rates (Continued)</div>
      <div style="margin-top: 15px;">
        <div class="line-item">
          <div class="label">27 Enter the amount from line 10.</div>
          <div class="value"><span data-field="line_27">{{ line_27 }}</span></div>
        </div>
        <div class="line-item">
          <div class="label">28 Enter the amount from your 1999 Schedule D (Form 1040), line 27 (or 1999 Schedule D (Form 1041), line 26).</div>
          <div class="value"><span data-field="line_28">{{ line_28 }}</span></div>
        </div>
        <div class="line-item">
          <div class="label">29 Enter the amount from your 1999 Schedule D (Form 1040), line 25 (or 1999 Schedule D (Form 1041), line 24).</div>
          <div class="value"><span data-field="line_29">{{ line_29 }}</span></div>
        </div>
        <div class="line-item">
          <div class="label">30 Add lines 28 and 29.</div>
          <div class="value"><span data-field="line_30">{{ line_30 }}</span></div>
        </div>
        <div class="line-item">
          <div class="label">31 Enter the amount from your 1999 Schedule D (Form 1040), line 22 (or 1999 Schedule D (Form 1041), line 21).</div>
          <div class="value"><span data-field="line_31">{{ line_31 }}</span></div>
        </div>
        <div class="line-item">
          <div class="label">32 Enter the smaller of line 30 or line 31.</div>
          <div class="value"><span data-field="line_32">{{ line_32 }}</span></div>
        </div>
        <div class="line-item">
          <div class="label">33 Subtract line 32 from line 27. If zero or less, enter -0.</div>
          <div class="value"><span data-field="line_33">{{ line_33 }}</span></div>
        </div>
        <div class="line-item">
          <div class="label">34 Multiply line 33 by 26% (26). If line 33 is: $175,000 or less if single, head of household, married filing jointly, qualifying widow(er), or an estate or trust for 1999; or $87,500 or less if married filing separately for 1999. Otherwise, multiply line 10 by 28% (28) and subtract from the result: $3,500 if single, head of household, married filing jointly, qualifying widow(er), or an estate or trust for 1999; or $1,750 if married filing separately for 1999.</div>
          <div class="value"><span data-field="line_34">{{ line_34 }}</span></div>
        </div>
        <div class="line-item">
          <div class="label">35 Enter the amount from your 1999 Schedule D (Form 1040), line 36 (or 1999 Schedule D (Form 1041), line 35). If you did not complete Part IV of your 1999 Schedule D (Form 1040) or an estate or trust, enter -0.</div>
          <div class="value"><span data-field="line_35">{{ line_35 }}</span></div>
        </div>
        <div class="line-item">
          <div class="label">36 Enter the smallest of line 27, line 28, or line 35.</div>
          <div class="value"><span data-field="line_36">{{ line_36 }}</span></div>
        </div>
        <div class="line-item">
          <div class="label">37 Multiply line 36 by 10% (10).</div>
          <div class="value"><span data-field="line_37">{{ line_37 }}</span></div>
        </div>
        <div class="line-item">
          <div class="label">38 Enter the smaller of line 27 or line 28.</div>
          <div class="value"><span data-field="line_38">{{ line_38 }}</span></div>
        </div>
        <div class="line-item">
          <div class="label">39 Enter the amount from line 36.</div>
          <div class="value"><span data-field="line_39">{{ line_39 }}</span></div>
        </div>
        <div class="line-item">
          <div class="label">40 Subtract line 39 from line 38. If zero or less, enter -0.</div>
          <div class="value"><span data-field="line_40">{{ line_40 }}</span></div>
        </div>
        <div class="line-item">
          <div class="label">41 Multiply line 40 by 20% (20).</div>
          <div class="value"><span data-field="line_41">{{ line_41 }}</span></div>
        </div>
        <div class="line-item">
          <div class="label">Note: If line 29 is zero or blank, skip lines 42 through 45 and go to line 46.</div>
          <div class="value"><span data-field="line_42">{{ line_42 }}</span></div>
        </div>
        <div class="line-item">
          <div class="label">42 Enter the amount from line 27.</div>
          <div class="value"><span data-field="line_43">{{ line_43 }}</span></div>
        </div>
        <div class="line-item">
          <div class="label">43 Add lines 33, 36, and 40.</div>
          <div class="value"><span data-field="line_44">{{ line_44 }}</span></div>
        </div>
        <div class="line-item">
          <div class="label">44 Subtract line 43 from line 42.</div>
          <div class="value"><span data-field="line_45">{{ line_45 }}</span></div>
        </div>
        <div class="line-item">
          <div class="label">45 Multiply line 44 by 25% (25).</div>
          <div class="value"><span data-field="line_46">{{ line_46 }}</span></div>
        </div>
        <div class="line-item">
          <div class="label">46 Add lines 34, 37, 41, and 45.</div>
          <div class="value"><span data-field="line_47">{{ line_47 }}</span></div>
        </div>
        <div class="line-item">
          <div class="label">47 Multiply line 27 by 26% (26). If line 27 is: $175,000 or less if single, head of household, married filing jointly, qualifying widow(er), or an estate or trust for 1999; or $87,500 or less if married filing separately for 1999. Otherwise, multiply line 10 by 28% (28) and subtract from the result: $3,500 if single, head of household, married filing jointly, qualifying widow(er), or an estate or trust for 1999; or $1,750 if married filing separately for 1999.</div>
          <div class="value"><span data-field="line_48">{{ line_48 }}</span></div>
        </div>
        <div class="line-item">
          <div class="label">48 Enter the smaller of line 46 or line 47 here and on line 11.</div>
          <div class="value"><span data-field="line_49">{{ line_49 }}</span></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div style="width: 50%; text-align: right;">
      <div style="font-size: 10pt;">Page 3</div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="page">
  <div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: flex-start;">
    <div style="width: 50%;">
      <div class="section-header">Line 12, is zero or less, enter zero on Form 8801, line 4. Otherwise, enter on line 12.</div>
      <div style="margin-top: 15px;">
        <div class="line-item">
          <div class="label">The allowance of the deduction for personal exemptions under section 641 is not attributable to exclusion items.</div>
          <div class="value"></div>
        </div>
        <div class="line-item">
          <div class="label">For loss years beginning before 1987, the amount of MTFCE that carried forward to tax years beginning after 1986 is equal to the amount of regular tax not paid that year.</div>
          <div class="value"></div>
        </div>
        <div class="line-item">
          <div class="label">To determine the amount of MTFCE that may be carried to tax years other than 1999, apply sections 6201 and 6202 with appropriate modifications to into exclusions items.</div>
          <div class="value"></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div style="width: 50%; text-align: right;">
      <div style="font-size: 10pt;">Page 4</div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="section-header" style="margin-top: 25px;">Line 1–Line 3 Estimates and Trusts</div>
  <div style="margin-top: 15px;">
    <div class="line-item">
      <div class="label">Skip lines 1 through 3 of Form 8801. Complete Parts I and II of Form 8801.</div>
      <div class="value"></div>
    </div>
    <div class="line-item">
      <div class="label">For Part III, take into account any adjustments arising from deferral items. If the amount on Schedule I, line 3 is this page for how to figure the amount to enter on line 11.</div>
      <div class="value"></div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="section-header" style="margin-top: 25px;">Line 4</div>
  <div style="margin-top: 15px;">
    <div class="line-item">
      <div class="label">If your filing status was married filing separately for 1999, enter the amount from Form 6251, line 30. If you were married filing jointly or qualifying widow(er) for 1999, enter the amount from Form 6251, line 31. If you were single or head of household for 1999, enter the amount from Form 6251, line 32.</div>
